`teamService.test.ts` has no tests for `createInvite` or `buildInviteLink`, which is why the inverted branch and the wrong returned token can slip through. The new e2e suite only creates non-org teams and never checks the link shape (`/teams` vs `/signup`). The PR checklist explicitly asks to confirm correct links for org sub-teams.

::code{file="apps/api/v2/src/modules/teams/invite/controllers/teams-invite.controller.e2e-spec.ts" lines="66-76"}

It would help to add an org sub-team case to the e2e tests and assert the URL path for both cases. Unit tests in `teamService.test.ts` should check that the returned `token` matches what was persisted.

`GetUser` is imported but never used in the controller:

::diff{file="apps/api/v2/src/modules/teams/invite/controllers/teams-invite.controller.ts" lines="1-7"}

The PR also strips the trailing newline from `teamService.ts`, which adds noise to the diff.
